Description: zink binds the whole last block of a sparse buffer
 ARB_sparse_buffer lets a commit reach the end of a buffer without being a
 whole number of pages. buffer_commit_single() cut the Vulkan bind to the
 buffer's size (width0), so the last bind of a buffer of 864 bytes, or of one
 with a partial last page, was 864 or 31424 bytes long. A Vulkan sparse bind is
 made of blocks of VkMemoryRequirements::alignment (65536 here) and the memory
 the buffer needs is that long. NVIDIA's proprietary driver ignored such a bind
 (the pages stayed unbacked and read as zero, without an error), and the
 validation layers report VUID-VkSparseMemoryBind-resourceOffset-09491.
 .
 It showed on the RTX 3060 (615.71.09) as a point cloud whose batch
 descriptors and point arrays read zero: the cloud loaded and drew nothing,
 beside the storage buffer bug of patch 0035. The bind now covers the whole
 last block, which is what the buffer's memory requirement is.
 .
 Tested by tests/egl-surfaceless-sparse-tail.c: red before (864 and 31424
 bytes read back as zero), green after, on zink over NVIDIA's Vulkan driver.
 Related: mesa#10220 (Paulo Zanoni, closed 2024-02-23) describes this bind
 and says NVIDIA's driver fails it; Mesa main (zink_bo.c, 2026-11-09) still
 has the MIN2 against width0.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-09
Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
---
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_bo.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_bo.c
@@ -829,7 +829,12 @@
 
    VkSparseMemoryBind mem_bind;
    mem_bind.resourceOffset = offset;
-   mem_bind.size = MIN2(res->base.b.width0 - offset, size);
+   /* GL lets a commit reach the end of the buffer without being a whole number of pages (ARB_sparse_buffer), but a Vulkan
+    * sparse bind is made of blocks of VkMemoryRequirements::alignment, and the memory the buffer needs is that long:
+    * bind the whole last block. NVIDIA's driver ignores a bind that stops inside a block (the pages stay unbacked and
+    * read as zero) and the validation layers report VUID-VkSparseMemoryBind-resourceOffset-09491.
+    */
+   mem_bind.size = MIN2(align64(res->base.b.width0, ZINK_SPARSE_BUFFER_PAGE_SIZE) - offset, size);
    mem_bind.memory = commit ? (bo->mem ? bo->mem : bo->u.slab.real->mem) : VK_NULL_HANDLE;
    mem_bind.memoryOffset = bo_offset * ZINK_SPARSE_BUFFER_PAGE_SIZE + (commit ? (bo->mem ? 0 : bo->offset) : 0);
    mem_bind.flags = 0;
